+### 4.3 list_sessions
+
+Asks for the conversations the connected user holds. There is no user id field on the frame, and that is the point: the list is always the connection's authenticated user's, whatever a client puts in the frame ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L58), [validated by: answers the connection user, session_list before pong](../../src/transport/ws/listSessionsSocket.test.ts#L31)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_sessions",
+  "limit": 10,
+  "before": {"updatedAt": "2026-01-01T00:05:00.000Z", "sessionId": "s3"}
+}
+```
+
+| Field    | Type   | Required | Description                                                              |
+| -------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_sessions"`                                                        |
+| `limit`  | number | No       | At most this many summaries to return                                    |
+| `before` | object | No       | Page cursor: the last row the client saw, as `updatedAt` and `sessionId` |
+
+Constraints:
+
+- `limit`, when present, MUST be a non-negative integer; any other shape of it is refused with an `INVALID_MESSAGE` error ([validated by: accepts list_sessions with an optional non-negative integer limit and a before cursor, dropping fields it does not define, and refuses any other limit or cursor shape](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L25)).
+- `before`, when present, MUST be an object whose `sessionId` is 1–128 characters and whose `updatedAt` is a timestamp — a string `Date.parse` accepts, or a finite epoch number; either half missing is refused as well ([validated by: accepts list_sessions with an optional non-negative integer limit and a before cursor, dropping fields it does not define, and refuses any other limit or cursor shape](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L25)).
+- Any other field is dropped rather than forwarded, a client-supplied `userId` included: the validator forwards only the fields the frame defines ([validated by: accepts list_sessions with an optional non-negative integer limit and a before cursor, dropping fields it does not define, and refuses any other limit or cursor shape](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L25)).
